{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDaily plan-review cache reads in `.rebar/usage.jsonl` fell from ~80% of input tokens (2026-08-06..11) to 0 from 2026-08-12, and the median full plan review rose from ~$2.18 to ~$4.82 (Aug 6–29 logged spend ~$3,000). The transition coincides with commit `6d4f394195b2` (2026-08-10, ticket `esthetical-earthborn-vervet` / `8fbd-e9d5-326e-40d8`), which added the Anthropic-direct fallback to the frontier/standard classes in `rebar.toml` `[llm.model_classes]`.\n\n`_intersect_capabilities` (`src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py`) computes ONE capability record for the whole fallback chain and collapses differing `prompt_cache_style` values to `\"none\"`. Both mixed chains are **Bedrock-primary, Anthropic-fallback** (`rebar.toml:223-224`), and the Anthropic hedge fires only **0.43%** of calls (51 of 11,902 logged rows), so the collapse disabled caching on the Bedrock target that serves ~99.6% of calls.\n\n## Why reversing the documented intent is sound (detail in ticket comment)\n\nThe collapse-to-none is documented/approved intent in three sites, all updated by this change: the `_intersect_capabilities` docstring (`runner_support.py:56-58`, where the \"keys would error on the non-sharing candidate\" premise lives), the `rebar.toml` `[llm.model_classes]` note (~190-193), and `docs/llm-framework.md` (~829-840). ADR 0059 §7 documents the per-provider key mechanics rather than that premise; it gets a superseding note, preserving §2's ModelProfile-not-provider-name invariant.\n\nThat premise is false for cache keys, proven at runtime: the cache directive is provider-scoped `ModelSettings` keys, `merge_model_settings` is an unvalidated dict union, and each provider model reads only its own `*_cache_*` keys via `.get(...)` — so a Bedrock-primary directive reaching a served Anthropic fallback is a silent no-op (uncached-but-correct), never an error. The full mechanism, runtime experiment, LangChain#37042 direction, and OSS grounding (LiteLLM, pydantic-ai) are in the pinned ticket comment.\n\nTherefore only `prompt_cache_style` — advisory and inert cross-provider — follows the PRIMARY; fields that CAN hard-fail cross-provider (`supports_temperature` → HTTP 400, `native_structured_output`, `supports_thinking`, `native_output_with_thinking`, `native_web_search`) stay conservatively `all(...)`-intersected.\n\n## Approach\n\nOption **(a): fix the capability seam** (operator decision; option (b), homogenising the chains, is off the table — the Anthropic hedge is required functionality). In `_intersect_capabilities`, derive `prompt_cache_style` from `per_candidate[0]` (the primary/serving candidate) instead of collapsing to `\"none\"`; keep every hard-failing field `all(...)`-intersected. Update the three stale-intent sites and ADR 0059 §7. The runtime analysis establishes (a) does not destabilise the seam, so no escalation.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py` — seam fix + docstring rewrite (stale-intent site 1).\n- `tests/unit/test_runner_support.py` — NEW focused module for `_intersect_capabilities` (defined in `runner_support.py`, so this is its natural home; `test_llm_capabilities.py` imports it via the `rebar.llm.runner` re-export for unrelated native-output-under-thinking assertions, left intact).\n- `rebar.toml` — `[llm.model_classes]` caching comment (site 2).\n- `docs/llm-framework.md` — mixed-provider-chain caching stanza (site 3).\n- `docs/adr/0059-llm-provider-seam-and-support-tiers.md` — superseding note in §7.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit (`tests/unit/test_runner_support.py`): a mixed Bedrock-primary chain keeps `\"bedrock\"` (RED before fix); an Anthropic-primary chain keeps `\"anthropic\"`; a `\"none\"`-primary chain stays `\"none\"`; a homogeneous chain is unchanged; hard-fail fields still intersect conservatively; and a parametrized fallback-fires test proves the primary directive is inert on the Anthropic arm. Mutation-checked: seeding the historical collapse-to-none turns 5 of 7 tests RED. Live check: a post-fix `review-plan` logs `cache_read_tokens > 0` in `.rebar/usage.jsonl`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A regression test proves a mixed Bedrock-primary chain reports `prompt_cache_style == \"bedrock\"` (not `\"none\"`); RED before the fix, green after; runs in `make test`.\n- [ ] A test proves a served Anthropic fallback receiving the Bedrock-primary directive reads every `anthropic_cache_*` key as `None` with no `UserError` (uncached-but-correct).\n- [ ] A regression test asserts `supports_temperature` and `native_structured_output` still withdraw (intersect conservatively) on a mixed chain.\n- [ ] The `_intersect_capabilities` docstring is updated to cache-follows-primary.\n- [ ] The `rebar.toml` `[llm.model_classes]` caching comment (~190-193) is updated to cache-follows-primary.\n- [ ] The `docs/llm-framework.md` caching stanza (~829-840) is updated to cache-follows-primary.\n- [ ] ADR 0059 §7 carries a superseding note recording cache-follows-serving-provider.\n- [ ] After the fix, a production plan review logs non-zero `cache_read_tokens` in `.rebar/usage.jsonl`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788036644274811001,"uuid":"4eeacc58-7d59-458a-8efb-8bf811a484ec"}